        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "41386c8f-2e35-5b4c-8a1d-2f2f7ef80129",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Levinson, William Link, Bruce Geller, Joe Mannix, Gail Fisher, Peggy Fair\n- Works: Mannix, Don't Eat the Babies, Island Fury\n- Roles: private investigator, secretary\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Geller was born on October 13, 1930, and died on May 21, 1978.\n- Bruce Geller was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\n- Mannix was created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller.\n- In Mannix, Joe Mannix is the title character and works as a private investigator.\n- Gail Fisher played secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series Mannix from 1968 through 1975.\n- Gail Fisher won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award for her role as Peggy Fair on Mannix.\n- Gail Fisher was the first black woman to win either a Golden Globe Award or an Emmy Award.\n- Don't Eat the Babies, also known as Island Fury, is a 1983 American horror and thriller film directed by Bruce Geller.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "68db6a91-178f-50b0-8dd9-7b5b42197b4d",
        "text": "Page: Mannix. Sentence: Created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller, the title character, Joe Mannix, is a private investigator.\nPage: Bruce Geller. Sentence: Bruce Bernard Geller (October 13, 1930 – May 21, 1978) was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\nPage: Gail Fisher. Sentence: She was best known for playing the role of secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series \"Mannix\" from 1968 through 1975, a role for which she won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award; she was the first black woman to win either award.\nPage: Please Don't Eat the Babies. Sentence: Don't Eat the Babies (also known as Island Fury) is a 1983 American horror and thriller film directed by Bruce Geller.",
